From: prep-task 2026-09-18
Subject: [PATCH] Qwen3.8-Flash-Next MTP: wire reduced-vocab draft head onto
 the dormant LocalArgmaxMixin

Qwen3_8FlashNextMTP already inherits LocalArgmaxMixin (get_top_tokens with
D2T remap), but nothing in mtp.py registers a draft_id_to_target_id table or
shrinks the draft lm_head -- confirmed by grep, also dormant for
deepseek_v32/nvidia/mtp.py and glm5next/nvidia/mtp.py in this fork. Without
a reduced head, --speculative-config use_local_argmax_reduction:true only
saves cross-rank communication (O(vocab)->O(2*tp_size)); it does not touch
the 1.18 GiB/rank full lm_head weight read per draft step that MiaAI-Lab's
external patch_mtp_draft_vocab.py targets.

This patch:
  - reads VLLM_QWEN_MTP_DRAFT_VOCAB_PATH (torch.save'd int64 tensor of
    target-vocab ids, length = draft_vocab_size, produced by
    scripts/build_draft_vocab.py)
  - hard-refuses to boot if the path is set without
    --speculative-config use_local_argmax_reduction:true (the
    compute_logits().argmax() fallback in
    vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/speculator.py _greedy_sample_draft would
    otherwise return draft-space ids as target ids -- silent corruption)
  - hard-refuses if config.tie_word_embeddings (same restriction as the
    existing NVFP4 draft head)
  - keeps the PRIMARY lm_head/logits_processor at full config.vocab_size so
    the checkpoint loads unmodified (b12x's checkpoint router rejects any
    shape mismatch between a checkpoint tensor and its declared param -- see
    "update 2" below, this is not a generic reshape/slice engine)
  - builds a SEPARATE draft_lm_head (ParallelLMHead sized draft_vocab_size),
    never touched by the checkpoint loader (it has no entry in the checkpoint
    stream), populated post-load in _populate_draft_lm_head(): all-gather the
    fully-loaded primary lm_head weight across TP, index_select the
    draft-vocab rows (in table order), re-shard into this rank's slice
  - overrides get_top_tokens() to route the draft argmax through
    draft_lm_head instead of the (full-vocab) primary lm_head, so
    LocalArgmaxMixin's D2T remap (k + draft_id_to_target_id[k]) lines up
    against a draft_vocab_size-wide k

MiaAI-Lab measured +8-21% on this model with their hand-rolled version;
this reuses vLLM's own tested LocalArgmaxMixin/get_top_tokens instead of
reimplementing it, per kernel-sweep-2026-09-18.md §4's recommendation
(path 2, "more native, avoids external AGPL patch dependency").

History (2026-09-18, dv arm, chronological):
  boot1 (original patch, resized primary lm_head + sliced-weight load):
    RuntimeError: Expected all tensors to be on the same device, but found
    at least two devices, cuda:0 and cpu! -- register_buffer(
    "draft_id_to_target_id", target_ids - torch.arange(self.draft_vocab_size,
    dtype=torch.int64), ...) built arange on CPU while target_ids (loaded via
    torch.load then moved to the model device) is already on cuda:0.
  boot2 (+ device=target_ids.device fix, primary lm_head still resized):
    NotImplementedError: checkpoint routing performed an unsupported data
    transformation (b12x/loader/_checkpoint.py:395) -- resizing the primary
    lm_head to draft_vocab_size and slicing the checkpoint lm_head.weight to
    match gives b12x's checkpoint router a declared param shape that does not
    match the checkpoint tensor shape at that name; it refuses the mismatch.
  boot3 (this version, primary head untouched + separate draft_lm_head):
    see the arm 3 gate report for the outcome.

Verified: git apply --check against local-inference-lab/vllm@8e1f1e587
(fork tip 2026-09-16) passes clean; result parses with ast.parse(); the
regenerated diff round-trips byte-identical against the hot-patched file that
was actually boot-tested in the -dv image (recipes/eugr/mods/vllm-dv-devicefix
ships that file directly and copies it into place -- no rebuild needed to
retest; fold into a rebuild only once this arm is gated and promoted).

